{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba22aeafb6a3f465a85408a2c2f7ba8141ffd0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I, T, E, S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> be distinct positive integers such that the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/029238b7d374b580706257bad8b312b21cc00ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ITEST  =  2006$\" width=\"122\" height=\"12\" />.  What is the largest possible value of the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f41eac55854dad3283ec482ea70946c73a8328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I  +  T  +  E  +  S  +  T  +  2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"212\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6bc0a9ccfebc35dec2173322cf1d71c72a8a9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\, 2086\\quad\\mathrm{(B)}\\, 4012\\quad\\mathrm{(C)}\\, 2144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the expression can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f467469cfa17044a2f109d2684b7559f9ff060a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IT^2ES = 2006$\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />.  The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1216dd3855e1bb88b6136b4ce49c58b57747417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29bf6058485d47006a70f340d0bfac936557884b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 17 \\cdot 59$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1216dd3855e1bb88b6136b4ce49c58b57747417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> does not have perfect squares as prime factors, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1277a7b531b016ef04a6921e11362b16a39d7fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />.  The other variables are the three primes since all variables are distinct, so the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f41eac55854dad3283ec482ea70946c73a8328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I  +  T  +  E  +  S  +  T  +  2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"212\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/2/8c24f02a67324c62ede2c629845ff56b919720f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 2 + 17 + 59 + 2006 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2086}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"287\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 iTest Pr